     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-06 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>ACB investigates suspicious transactions at LB Nagar fire station</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Anti-Corruption Bureau (ACB) detected approximately 90 suspicious UPI transactions ranging from ₹1,000 to ₹4,500 on the mobile phones of LB Nagar fire station staff. The investigation follows allegations that personnel charged more than the prescribed ₹500 fee for temporary firecracker shop licenses. Bureau officials are currently probing these transactions and examining reasons for delays in processing 397 received applications.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-06/acb-investigates-suspicious-transactions-at-lb-nagar-fire-st.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The ACB has urged the public to report any demands for excess fees or unexplained processing delays. Citizens can reach out via the bureau's toll-free number 1064 or its designated WhatsApp number 9440446106 to file complaints regarding the ongoing matter.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is concise, accurate, and includes all relevant figures and contact details provided in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/telangana/acb-detects-90-suspicious-upi-transactions-at-lb-nagar-fire-station/article71675894.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
