       <h1>Army, Navy Offices to Relocate from South Block by Early December</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Army</span> <span>#Navy</span> <span>#South Block</span> <span>#Relocation</span></div>
       <p>A major relocation exercise is underway for the Indian Army and Navy offices, which are set to shift their operations out of the historic South Block. This significant move is scheduled to be completed by early December, according to a report from The Times of India.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-06/army-navy-offices-to-relocate-from-south-block-by-early-dece.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The exercise involves central defence offices vacating their long-standing premises. The precise details of their new locations were not specified in the report.</p><p>What to watch: The timely completion of this major office relocation.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately conveys the provided source summary but is quite brief; however, it exhausts the limited information provided in the source.</p>
