       <h1>Bar Council of India Removes Age Limit for Law Studies</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Education</span> <span>#Law</span> <span>#India</span></div>
       <p>The Bar Council of India has announced a significant change, opening doors for aspirants of all age groups to study law. This decision removes previous restrictions that may have prevented older individuals from pursuing a legal education.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-06/bar-council-of-india-removes-age-limit-for-law-studies.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The new policy clarifies that there will be no age limit for individuals wishing to enroll in law programs. This move by the Bar Council of India aims to broaden access to legal education across the country.</p><p>What to watch: Impact on law school admissions.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate summary of the provided source material.</p>
