     <article class="story single" data-beat="business">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">BUSINESS</span> · Business Standard · 2026-11-06 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Benchmark Indices Advance as IT Shares Rise; Broader Markets Decline</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Stock Market</span> <span>#Sensex</span> <span>#Nifty</span> <span>#IT Shares</span></div>
       <p>Benchmark indices advanced on Friday, November 6, 2026, driven by a rise in IT shares amid the unwinding of global AI-trade bets. As of 12:00 PM, the Sensex climbed 450.38 points, or 0.57 per cent, to reach 79,760.39, while the Nifty50 was up 77.90 points, or 0.32 per cent, at 24,614.50.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-06/benchmark-indices-advance-as-it-shares-rise-broader-markets-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>In the broader markets, the Nifty MidCap 100 experienced a fall of 0.93 per cent, and the Nifty SmallCap 100 declined by 1.54 per cent. Among the Nifty50 components, Hindalco Industries, Shriram Finance, and Asian Paints were identified as the top losers during the trading session.</p><p>Sector-wise, the Nifty IT index led the gains, rising 1 per cent and outperforming its peers. This uplift was attributed to a boost in sentiment for domestic shares as investors unwound bets on global AI-linked equities. Conversely, several other sectors underperformed, including Nifty Metal, Nifty Realty, Nifty PSU Bank, and Nifty Oil and Gas.</p><p>Numerous companies are scheduled to release their Q2 results on Friday, including 3M India, AJAX Engineering, The Anup Engineering, Aster DM Quality Care, Azad Engineering, Blue Dart Express, Bluspring Enterprises, Bombay Dyeing &amp; Manufacturing Company, Bosch, AvenuesAI, Cholamandalam Financial Holdings, Cohance Lifesciences, Data Patterns (India), Dynamatic Technologies, Elgi Equipments, Gland Pharma, Godrej Agrovet, Hindalco Industries, Hindustan Oil Exploration Company, Honasa Consumer, Ingersoll-Rand (India), Jubilant FoodWorks, Kirloskar Industries, Nuvama Wealth Management, Precision Wires India, Prism Johnson, Rain Industries, Ratnamani Metals &amp; Tubes, Repco Home Finance, Rossell Techsys, Scoda Tubes, Siemens, Sirca Paints India, Star Cement, Supriya Lifescience, TTK Prestige, Voltas, and Vardhman Textiles.</p><p>What to watch: The impact of Q2 results on individual stock performance and sector trends.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately reports market data, sector performance, and the full list of companies releasing Q2 results as provided in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.business-standard.com/markets/news/stock-market-live-november-6-nse-bse-sensex-today-nifty50-gift-nifty-crude-oil-prices-q2-results-today-dhanteras-126110600099_1.html" rel="noopener">Business Standard</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
