       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-06 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Cyberabad Police evaluate one-way traffic plan for HITEC City</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Cyberabad Police are exploring a one-way traffic system across the Biodiversity, Mindspace, and HITEC City corridors to alleviate severe peak-hour congestion. Commissioner of Police M. Ramesh led an inspection of the proposed route, which includes IKEA, T-Works, and Qualcomm, to assess traffic flow and identify bottlenecks. The initiative aims to streamline vehicular movement near major tech hubs and commercial centers.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-06/cyberabad-police-evaluate-one-way-traffic-plan-for-hitec-cit.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Officials have been directed to conduct a comprehensive study, including a block-wise assessment of buildings to determine their specific impact on traffic volume. The resulting report will document parking availability and potential conflict points to help determine the feasibility of the proposed one-way traffic management strategy.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively summarizes the scope of the police inspection and the goals of the proposed traffic study.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/cities/Hyderabad/cyberabad-police-explore-one-way-traffic-system-across-biodiversity-hitec-city-corridors/article71675124.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
