       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">HEALTH</span> · ET Healthworld · 2026-11-06 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Fortis Hospital Business Sees Revenue Growth, Profit Decline in Q2 FY27</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Healthcare</span> <span>#Business</span> <span>#Finance</span> <span>#Earnings</span></div>
       <p>Fortis' hospital business reported an 18.6 percent year-on-year (YoY) growth in revenue, reaching Rs 2,340 crore for the second quarter of Fiscal Year 2027 (Q2 FY27). This indicates strong top-line performance.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-06/fortis-hospital-business-sees-revenue-growth-profit-decline-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Despite the revenue increase, the Profit After Tax (PAT) for the hospital segment experienced a slight decline of 1.1 percent YoY, settling at Rs 284 crore. This suggests a compression in profit margins.</p><p>Occupancy rates at Fortis hospitals saw a modest improvement, rising to 72 percent in Q2 FY27 from 71 percent in the previous year. This slight increase points to stable patient footfall.</p><p>What to watch: Future strategies for profit margin improvement.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft effectively captures all data points from the source summary and presents them clearly without unnecessary padding.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://health.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/hospitals/fortis-posts-2735-crore-in-q2-fy27-profit-dips-2-5/135590500" rel="noopener">ET Healthworld</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
