     <article class="story single" data-beat="tech">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">TECH</span> · Engadget · 2026-11-06 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Gentle Monster to Open Pre-orders for Google-Powered Intelligent Eyewear</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#tech</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Gentle Monster announced that its &quot;Intelligent Eyewear,&quot; developed on Google's Android XR platform, will be available for pre-order on November 12. The wearable, which features an audio-first, display-free design with Gemini integration, is scheduled for a December launch. The company teased the release with a promotional film starring Joaquin Phoenix and directed by Jonathan Glazer.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-06/gentle-monster-to-open-pre-orders-for-google-powered-intelli.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This project, which includes Warby Parker and Samsung as partners, aims to compete with Meta’s smart glasses. While Google has not officially confirmed the release dates, these upcoming launches represent a strategic move to integrate technology into fashion-forward eyewear brands.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is accurate, concise, and correctly attributes the information to the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
