     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-06 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Kerala Excise Commissioner Transferred Amid Licensing Dispute</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Kerala Excise Commissioner Seeram Sambasiva Rao has been transferred, following public criticism from Excise Minister M. Liju regarding the unauthorized granting of bar licenses. The Minister expressed disapproval over licenses issued to a Kochi airport lounge without government consultation.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-06/kerala-excise-commissioner-transferred-amid-licensing-disput.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Minister Liju indicated the government is investigating whether officials used procedural loopholes to expedite approvals ahead of a new excise policy. Chief Minister V.D. Satheesan confirmed that no bar licenses should be issued without government oversight. The Additional Excise Commissioner has assumed charge of the post.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurately captures the transfer of the Excise Commissioner and the context of the licensing dispute.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/kerala/keralam-excise-commissioner-seeram-sambasiva-rao-shifted-amid-differences-with-minister-over-bar-licence/article71673257.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
