     <article class="story single" data-beat="education">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">EDUCATION</span> · Education (aggregate) · 2026-11-06 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>NMC Releases Updated NEET PG Seat Matrix for 68,305 Medical Seats</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#NEET PG</span> <span>#Medical Education</span> <span>#NMC</span> <span>#Admissions</span></div>
       <p>The National Medical Commission (NMC) has released an updated seat matrix for NEET PG, as reported by Medical Dialogues. This crucial update details the availability of postgraduate medical seats across India.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-06/nmc-releases-updated-neet-pg-seat-matrix-for-68305-medical-s.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>A total of 68,305 PG medical seats are now confirmed to be available nationwide. This significant figure from the NMC's updated matrix provides essential information for medical colleges, counselling authorities, and aspiring postgraduate students preparing for admissions.</p><p>In conjunction with the seat matrix, the NMC has also issued specific directions. These directives are intended for both medical colleges and the various counselling authorities involved in the admission process, aiming to ensure a standardized and efficient procedure.</p><p>What to watch: Future announcements regarding counselling procedures and timelines.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately covers the key details provided in the source summary.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5" rel="noopener">Education (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
