       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-06 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Parents Remain Wary Following Andhra School Chainsaw Attack</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Parents of students at the ZPHS school in Andhra Pradesh continue to express safety concerns following a violent chainsaw attack on a Class 10 student on October 31. Despite the immediate arrest of the accused and proactive counseling services provided by the Education Department and local police, community anxiety remains high.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-06/parents-remain-wary-following-andhra-school-chainsaw-attack.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The incident has left a lasting impact on the school environment, with many families hesitant to return their wards to the premises. Authorities have attempted to stabilize the situation through institutional support, but the psychological scars of the assault persist among the student body and their guardians.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the situation in Andhra Pradesh based on the provided source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
