       <h1>Quad Navies Begin Malabar War Games Off Japan, Focus on Sub-hunting</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Quad</span> <span>#Malabar Exercise</span> <span>#Naval Drills</span> <span>#Japan</span></div>
       <p>The navies of the Quadrilateral Security Dialogue (Quad) nations have commenced the Malabar war games, as reported by The New Indian Express. This significant multinational exercise brings together naval forces from the Quad member countries to enhance maritime cooperation and interoperability.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-06/quad-navies-begin-malabar-war-games-off-japan-focus-on-sub-h.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The current iteration of the drills is taking place off the coast of Japan. A primary focus of this year's Malabar exercise is on sub-hunting operations, indicating a concentrated effort to bolster anti-submarine warfare capabilities and coordination among the participating forces.</p><p>What to watch: Further details on specific exercises and joint capabilities demonstrated during the war games.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft concisely and accurately reflects the information provided in the source summary.</p>
