     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-06 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Supreme Court Awards Himachal Pradesh 11,973 MU of Electricity</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Supreme Court of India has settled a decades-old dispute, directing Punjab and Haryana to supply Himachal Pradesh with 11,973 million units of electricity over 20 years. Chief Minister Sukhvinder Singh Sukhu hailed the ruling as a historic victory for the state’s financial rights.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-06/supreme-court-awards-himachal-pradesh-11973-mu-of-electricit.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This allocation from the Bhakra-Nangal and Beas hydroelectric projects is expected to generate up to ₹1,000 crore in annual revenue. The state government plans to invest these funds into healthcare, education, road infrastructure, and employment initiatives to support its 75 lakh residents.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is accurate and captures the core figures and context from the source text effectively.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/himachal-pradesh/supreme-court-decision-on-bbmb-arrears-a-victory-for-himachal-says-cm-sukhu/article71675039.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
