       <h1>Veterinarian Urges Diwali Safety Measures for Community Animals</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#positive</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Veterinarian Dr. Vikas Godara warns that Diwali firecrackers pose severe risks to community animals, including noise-induced anxiety, physical injuries, and gastrointestinal issues from discarded food. Experts note that street animals lack the safe retreats available to pets, often suffering from disorientation and fatal accidents near traffic. </p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-06/veterinarian-urges-diwali-safety-measures-for-community-anim.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Residents are encouraged to monitor animal feeding areas, avoid bursting crackers near resting spots, and report injuries to rescue organizations. While public awareness of animal distress is increasing, collective community action remains essential to prevent cruelty and ensure the safety of stray animals during the festive season.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately synthesizes the veterinary advice and community-based solutions while capturing the key risks identified by the source.</p>
